Chapter: RecordLayoutProbe

 A record with two field widths, ordered so that the two layouts in
 emit-record disagree about which slot holds the pointer.

   flag  : Boolean     -- field-byte-width 1, name sorts FIRST
   items : List Integer -- field-byte-width 8, name sorts SECOND

 Resolved layout (build-cce-byte-offsets, ranked by field-sort-key =
 width-prefix & name, offsets = cumulative widths):

   items @ 0   flag @ 8    size 9

 Fallback layout (emit-store-record-fields-by-list, ranked by raw name,
 offsets = rank * 8):

   flag  @ 0   items @ 8   size 16

 Readers always use the resolved rule (cce-byte-offset-and-type), so a Box
 built through the fallback puts `flag` where `items` is read from. Reading
 b.items then yields the boolean -- 0 or 1 -- and list-length of that reads
 [0 - 8] or [1 - 8], which is a page fault with CR2 near the top of the
 address space.

 Expected output: 3

Section: Types

  Box = record {
   flag : Boolean,
   items : List Integer
  }

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let b = Box { flag = True, items = [1, 2, 3] }
    in print-line-uni (show (list-length (b.items)))
  end
